question:
Which analytic inputs, if any, occur in this recorded row? Suppose $p$ is odd, $C/\overline{\F}_p$ has genus at least two,
and $G\subset\Aut(C)$ has order prime to $p$. Put $Y=C/G$ and
suppose $g(Y)\le2$. If at least one of the following holds, then
$C$ has a connected finite 'etale cover with prime-to-$p$ Galois
closure mapping to a supersingular curve of genus at least two:
 egin{enumerate}
\item $g(Y)=1$ or $2$;
\item $G$ is solvable;
\item two distinct branch values of $C	o Y$ have ramification
indices with a common prime factor.
\end{enumerate}
In particular this proves B5 for every tamely superelliptic curve
in every odd characteristic, including characteristic three.

Which analytic inputs, if any, occur in this recorded row? A complete vanishing test over number fields. For each $v
otin S$, let $e_{v,1},\ldots,e_{v,s_v}$ be the valuations of the nonzero Smith entries of $D_v$ on $A_v$. A unit entry has valuation zero; a zero Smith entry is excluded. The following conditions are equivalent:
 egin{enumerate}[label=(oman*)]
\item $\varprojlim{}^1 H^1(G_L,M/\ell^n)=0$;
\item the tower $P_n$ in F.2 is Mittag--Leffler;
\item the nonnegative integers $e_{v,i}$ are bounded, uniformly over $v$ and $i$;
\item the finite groups
\[
 B_v=
  rac{H^0(\mathbb F_v,A_v\otimes\mathbb Q_\ell/\mathbb Z_\ell)}
      {H^0(\mathbb F_v,A_v\otimes\mathbb Q_\ell/\mathbb Z_\ell)_{\mathrm{div}}}
\]
have uniformly bounded orders.
\end{enumerate}
The subscript $\mathrm{div}$ denotes the maximal divisible subgroup. No boundedness condition on the orders of $H^2(G_{L,S},M/\ell^n)$ is required. Their contribution to the full group is exactly the left term of (F.2.1).
